The repo entries below contain setups for the live, hot-off-the-presses 
yum repositories for Alpha Core updates and extras that have been built 
with a fancy new copy of the Fedora build system. I'd appreciate hearing 
success/horror stories regarding the packages in these repositories.

All packages are signed using the updates key, available here: 
http://ftp.alphacore.info/alpha/core/3/os/RPM-GPG-KEY-ac-updates

Packages in updates: 
http://genuine-article.alphacore.info/live/testing/updates/3/alpha/repodata/

Packages in extras:
http://genuine-article.alphacore.info/live/testing/extras/3/alpha/repodata/

("yum install vlc" should be possible very soon!)

-----
[updates-testing]
name=Alpha Core $releasever - Updates Testing
baseurl=http://genuine-article.alphacore.info/live/testing/updates/$releasever/$basearch
enabled=1
gpgcheck=1

[extras-testing]
name=Alpha Core $releasever - Extras Testing
baseurl=http://genuine-article.alphacore.info/live/testing/extras/$releasever/$basearch
enabled=1
gpgcheck=1



